@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Frequently asked questions"; }
<section class="page-hero"><span class="eyebrow">GOOD QUESTIONS</span><h1>Let's clear a few <em>things up.</em></h1><p>What LinkShield can do, what it cannot do, and how to use it thoughtfully.</p></section><section class="faq-list"><details open><summary>Does a low risk score mean the link is safe?</summary><p>No. The score only reflects the rules implemented in this project. A new or targeted threat may not trigger any of them.</p></details><details><summary>Does LinkShield open or visit the submitted website?</summary><p>No. This demo analyzes the text of the URL only. It does not visit the destination, download files, or query a commercial reputation service.</p></details><details><summary>What does the risk score mean?</summary><p>Each configured warning pattern adds points. The total is capped at 100 and grouped into Low, Medium, or High categories. It is a learning aid, not a scientific probability.</p></details><details><summary>Where is scan history stored?</summary><p>Scan records are saved to the configured MySQL database through Entity Framework Core.</p></details><details><summary>Can I use this for real cybersecurity decisions?</summary><p>Use it for awareness and demonstration only. Verify links through official channels and use trusted security tools for real-world protection.</p></details><details><summary>Why does a URL need http:// or https://?</summary><p>The full URL format allows the app to parse the scheme and hostname consistently for its checks.</p></details></section><div class="center-cta"><a class="btn btn-primary" asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Index">Try the scanner ↗</a></div>
